---
import {
    Monitor,
    Gauge,
    PackageOpen,
    Settings,
    UserGroup,
    ArrowRight,
    ArrowUpRight,
    Download,
    Plus,
} from "@lucide/astro";
---

<section
    id="faq"
    class="bg-amber-50/40 border-y border-amber-100/60 px-4 py-20 md:py-28"
>
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <div class="reveal text-center mb-12">
            <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 tracking-tight mb-4">
                A Few Things to Know.
            </h2>

            <p class="text-gray-600 text-lg">
                The practical details, without the mysterious Linux rituals.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-4">
            <details class="reveal reveal-delay-1 group rounded-xl bg-white border border-amber-100 p-5 sm:p-6">
                <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-gray-900">
                    What is BakeryOS?
                    <Plus />
                </summary>
                <p class="mt-4 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                    BakeryOS is an Arch-based Linux distribution focused on a
                    customized GNOME desktop, project-maintained packages, and
                    an integrated desktop experience.
                </p>
            </details>

            <details class="reveal reveal-delay-2 group rounded-xl bg-white border border-amber-100 p-5 sm:p-6">
                <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-gray-900">
                    Is BakeryOS based on Arch Linux?
                    <Plus />
                </summary>
                <p class="mt-4 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                    Yes. BakeryOS builds on the Arch Linux ecosystem and adds
                    its own packages, desktop configuration, and system
                    integration.
                </p>
            </details>

            <details class="reveal reveal-delay-3 group rounded-xl bg-white border border-amber-100 p-5 sm:p-6">
                <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-gray-900">
                    Who is BakeryOS for?
                    <Plus />
                </summary>
                <p class="mt-4 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                    BakeryOS is for people interested in a customized Linux
                    desktop, from everyday users willing to learn Linux to
                    developers who value flexibility and control.
                </p>
            </details>

            <details class="reveal reveal-delay-4 group rounded-xl bg-white border border-amber-100 p-5 sm:p-6">
                <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-gray-900">
                    Is BakeryOS free and open source?
                    <Plus />
                </summary>
                <p class="mt-4 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                    Review the licenses published with the project and its
                    individual components for the applicable terms of use,
                    modification, and redistribution.
                </p>
            </details>

            <details class="reveal reveal-delay-5 group rounded-xl bg-white border border-amber-100 p-5 sm:p-6">
                <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-gray-900">
                    How do I install BakeryOS?
                    <Plus />
                </summary>
                <p class="mt-4 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                    Visit the download page to find an available release, then
                    follow the installation documentation. Back up your files
                    before making disk or partition changes.
                </p>
            </details>

            <details class="reveal reveal-delay-6 group rounded-xl bg-white border border-amber-100 p-5 sm:p-6">
                <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-gray-900">
                    Where can I report a bug or contribute?
                    <Plus />
                </summary>
                <p class="mt-4 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                    Visit the BakeryOS project repository to explore the source
                    code, review existing issues, and find the appropriate place
                    to contribute.
                </p>
            </details>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
